   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation to\npermitting village justices of the village of Spring Valley to live in the\ntowns of Ramapo or Clarkstown",
    "basePrintNo": "S9082",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9082-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3-300, Vil L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S9082\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the village law and the public offi-\ncers law, in relation to permitting village justices of the village of\nSpring Valley to live in the towns of Ramapo or Clarkstown\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nPermits village justices of the village of Spring Valley to live in the\ntowns of Ramapo or the town of Clarkstown.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe Public Officers Law is amended by adding a new subdivision 57 and\n\nSection 3-300 of the village law is amended by adding a new subdivision\n19 to permit village justices of the village of Spring Valley to live in\nthe towns of Ramapo or the town of Clarkstown.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, the village of Spring Valley has two residency\noptions for village justices; this presents a problem for Spring Valley\nin that the candidate pool for qualified individuals seeking a position\nas a Village Justice is too small. This legislation will expand the\nresidence requirement, allowing more qualified options for Village\nJustice.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
